{"version":"1","id":"itssecurityyall","handle":"itssecurityyall","name":"It's Security Y'all!","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/42a6d46986f24231890eca5f58130560","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-7.6077,"y":-4.6008,"cluster_id":1,"posts_collected":64,"newest_post_at":"2024-01-17T20:25:52.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2023-11-01T18:48:49.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.132812,"listicle_ratio":0.0,"question_ratio":0.078125,"avg_read_time":2.75,"summary_length_avg":309.671875,"title_length_avg":57.0,"title_length_var":598.84375,"tag_entropy":2.413039,"tag_diversity":0.4375,"top_tag_share":0.703125,"avg_upvotes":0.234375,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.0,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.0625,"zero_engagement_share":0.8125,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":6.436587,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":64.0},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-7.4853,-9.2353],"cadence_depth":[-2.8529,-6.7941],"hype_variety":[9.5882,-7.0147],"title_style":[7.9412,-7.5735]},"top_tags":[["security",47],["cyber",34],["malware",21],["ransomware",14],["data-breach",10],["vulnerability",9],["phishing",8],["authentication",4]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["WTF happened last week?!?","Chrome Users Beware: Critical Zero-Day Vulnerability Discovered","SysJoker: A New Malware Threat to Watch Out For"],"outlier":["Hold Your Mamas, Y'all! Hospital Software Hit by Cyber Critters, Medical Records Leakin' Like a Rusty Bucket"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"7LHYlLxed","title":"Bigpanzi","url":"https://itssecurityyall.substack.com/p/bigpanzi","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/bigpanzi-7lhyllxed","summary":"Bigpanzi is a cybercrime syndicate that infects devices through firmware updates and backdoored apps. They use botnets for illegal streaming, traffic proxying, DDoS attacks, and content counterfeiting. Bigpanzi has custom malware including Pandoraspear and Pcdn. Security researchers are actively working to dismantle the Bigpanzi network.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/82ab654f47cfe5ced2bc0dbec18855f1?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-01-17T20:25:52.000Z"},{"id":"FW6PuYiUy","title":"Chrome Catches a Critter","url":"https://itssecurityyall.substack.com/p/chrome-catches-a-critter","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/chrome-catches-a-critter-fw6puyiuy","summary":"Chrome browser patched a zero-day exploit in the V8 engine and fixed two other V8 engine flaws. Microsoft Edge is also working on a patch. Other Chromium-based browsers are expected to receive fixes soon.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/4773bcaeb1b0d7aeea3867b766df5061?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-01-17T16:25:16.000Z"},{"id":"m9MQ5ysIR","title":"Shady Stealers Snatch Data with Windows Flaw","url":"https://itssecurityyall.substack.com/p/shady-stealers-snatch-data-with-windows","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/shady-stealers-snatch-data-with-windows-flaw-m9mq5ysir","summary":"New malware called Phemedrone Stealer is exploiting a previously patched Windows vulnerability to steal personal data. Users are advised to update their Windows immediately to secure their systems.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/8e28bde70658cd425db41fcd070845a8?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-01-15T17:29:51.000Z"},{"id":"TiPucsqmV","title":"Ivanti Under Attack","url":"https://itssecurityyall.substack.com/p/ivanti-under-attack","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/ivanti-under-attack-tipucsqmv","summary":"Hackers exploited hidden flaws in Ivanti Connect Secure, deploying snooping malware that intercepted network traffic, stole files, and enabled remote control of systems. Additional security measures are necessary to protect against lingering threats.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/82b0a52d30c1e9e3ff3d05b591fb3146?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-01-12T17:19:12.000Z"},{"id":"FKsehkKtP","title":"The Balada Bait & Switch","url":"https://itssecurityyall.substack.com/p/the-balada-bait-and-switch","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-balada-bait-switch-fksehkktp","summary":"The Balada Injector malware has hijacked over 6,700 WordPress websites, exploiting a vulnerability in the Popup Builder plugin. It redirects visitors to fake popups, lottery scams, and push notification spam traps. To protect your website, keep your plugins and themes updated and be cautious of suspicious redirections.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/6401adba0bc5b70856fffb691cda9f78?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-01-11T18:49:31.000Z"},{"id":"1yw9GthNE","title":"The Great X Caper","url":"https://itssecurityyall.substack.com/p/the-great-x-caper","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-great-x-caper-1yw9gthne","summary":"Hackers took over verified accounts, including Mandiant's X account, and used them to spread fake token airdrop scams, draining over $900,000 from crypto wallets. Users are advised to secure their accounts with two-factor authentication and be vigilant against phishing scams.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/776c2c1fe05b715f5560ffa9afe99686?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-01-11T14:36:14.000Z"},{"id":"2RS7OM5i6","title":"Babuk's Bad Day","url":"https://itssecurityyall.substack.com/p/babuks-bad-day","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/babuk-s-bad-day-2rs7om5i6","summary":"Dutch police arrested the operator of Tortilla ransomware and obtained a decryptor for victims' locked files. Other ransomware variants similar to Babuk and Tortilla are Rook, Night Sky, and AstraLocker. Avast provides a free decryptor for Tortilla and other Babuk variants.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/a6689884b983047c8951cb921a22fc38?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-01-09T17:51:48.000Z"},{"id":"yeazFh57n","title":"WTF happened last week?!?","url":"https://itssecurityyall.substack.com/p/wtf-happened-last-week-418","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/wtf-happened-last-week--yeazfh57n","summary":"The post discusses various security issues and vulnerabilities, including the revival of expired Google cookies by hackers, the exploitation of the MSIX flaw, and the bypassing of MFA methods by hackers.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/86d7ad37b0f1678bcf0c48232b8af8a8?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-12-31T14:47:29.000Z"},{"id":"ro8RnTjoy","title":"Digital Catfishin'!","url":"https://itssecurityyall.substack.com/p/digital-catfishin","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/digital-catfishin--ro8rntjoy","summary":"Hackers can gain access to Google accounts even after password changes by exploiting hidden login gates called 'MultiLogin'. Patching software, being cautious about downloads, and reporting suspicious activity can help protect against these attacks.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/473febc7bb44d330ee2e92c4a8cbdcd8?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-12-29T17:44:02.000Z"},{"id":"nvSEPB7Om","title":"From Emotet to Ransomware","url":"https://itssecurityyall.substack.com/p/from-emotet-to-ransomware","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/from-emotet-to-ransomware-nvsepb7om","summary":"Hackers exploited a vulnerability in the MSIX Flaw to install malware disguised as software or fake Microsoft Teams messages, posing ransomware risk. Users should update their Windows App Installer or disable the \"EnableMSAppInstallerProtocol\" setting. Stay vigilant and avoid downloading suspicious content.","image":"http